{"id":"ebc1e7645586f173","group":"58","path":"58/batch12/58-df-borel-cantelli.md","title":"Borel-Cantelli Lemma","display":"df-borel-cantelli — Borel-Cantelli Lemma","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-borel-cantelli","aliases":["58-df-borel-cantelli","Borel-Cantelli Lemma"],"display":"df-borel-cantelli — Borel-Cantelli Lemma","depends_on":["[[58-df-measure]]","[[58-df-measure-space]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-borel-cantelli"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-borel-cantelli</span><span>Borel-Cantelli Lemma</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-borel-cantelli — Borel-Cantelli Lemma"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ca832ed6bc22f728\" href=\"?note=ca832ed6bc22f728\" title=\"58-df-measure\">58-df-measure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"58-df-measure-space\">58-df-measure-space</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\">\\(\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\\)</span> (measure-space predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"83a15c7e9b3817dc\" href=\"?note=83a15c7e9b3817dc\" title=\"58-df-measure-space\">58-df-measure-space</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A:\\omega\\to\\mathcal F\">\\(A:\\omega\\to\\mathcal F\\)</span> (sequence of measurable events)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mu\">\\(\\mu\\)</span> (measure; probability normalization is not required)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BorelCantelliI}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{BorelCantelliI}_S\\)</span> (first Borel-Cantelli implication predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}borel\\text{-}cantelli} \\vdash \\mathrm{BorelCantelliI}_S(A,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\\land A\\in\\mathcal F^\\omega\\land\\left(\\sum_{n\\in\\omega}\\mu(A(n))&lt;\\infty\\to \\mu\\left(\\bigcap_{N\\in\\omega}\\bigcup_{n\\geq N}A(n)\\right)=0\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}borel\\text{-}cantelli} \\vdash \\mathrm{BorelCantelliI}_S(A,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\\land A\\in\\mathcal F^\\omega\\land\\left(\\sum_{n\\in\\omega}\\mu(A(n))&lt;\\infty\\to \\mu\\left(\\bigcap_{N\\in\\omega}\\bigcup_{n\\geq N}A(n)\\right)=0\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Borel-Cantelli: finite measure sum implies limsup measure zero</li>\n<li>&quot;i.o.&quot;: infinitely often</li>\n<li>Second BC: requires independence for converse</li>\n<li>If the events are independent and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sum_n\\mu(A(n))=\\infty\">\\(\\sum_n\\mu(A(n))=\\infty\\)</span>, the second Borel-Cantelli lemma gives probability one to the limsup event.</li>\n<li>The second Borel-Cantelli lemma and limsup-event definition should be separate atoms.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Billingsley, Probability and Measure</li>\n<li>Durrett, Probability: Theory and Examples</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-measure","status":"resolved","id":"ca832ed6bc22f728","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measure]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-measure-space","status":"resolved","id":"83a15c7e9b3817dc","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-measure-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-measure-space","status":"resolved","id":"83a15c7e9b3817dc","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mu)$ (measure-space predicate, see [[58-df-measure-space]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mu)","display":false},{"tex":"A:\\omega\\to\\mathcal F","display":false},{"tex":"\\mu","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BorelCantelliI}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}borel\\text{-}cantelli} \\vdash \\mathrm{BorelCantelliI}_S(A,\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{MeasureSpace}_S(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mu)\\land A\\in\\mathcal F^\\omega\\land\\left(\\sum_{n\\in\\omega}\\mu(A(n))<\\infty\\to \\mu\\left(\\bigcap_{N\\in\\omega}\\bigcup_{n\\geq N}A(n)\\right)=0\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\sum_n\\mu(A(n))=\\infty","display":false}],"bytes":1447,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-196","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-borel-cantelli.md|58-df-borel-cantelli]]（batch12）"}],"outgoing":["ca832ed6bc22f728","83a15c7e9b3817dc"]}